 			<p>“Not from you; it doesn’t sound natural, and I like your old bluntness better.”</p>
 			<p>“I’m glad of it,” he answered, with a look of relief; then buttoned her gloves for her, and asked if his tie was straight, just as he used to do when they went to parties together, at home.</p>
 			<p>The company assembled in the long <i xml:lang="fr">salle à manger</i>, that evening, was such as one sees nowhere but on the Continent. The hospitable Americans had invited every acquaintance they had in Nice, and, having no prejudice against titles, secured a few to add lustre to their Christmas ball.</p>
